The ALFWorld task pack plays games from the ALFWorld text environment
(https://github.com/alfworld/alfworld, MIT License, Copyright 2020 Mohit Shridhar,
Xingdi Yuan, Marc-Alexandre Côté, Yonatan Bisk, Adam Trischler, Matthew Hausknecht),
which builds on TextWorld (MIT) and AI2-THOR / ALFRED data. The game files are
generated upstream by `alfworld-download` (json_2.1.1, ALFRED data) and are not
redistributed in this repository; only deterministic game-path selection is encoded
here, so each machine regenerates the identical pack from its local ALFWorld cache.
The runner, evaluator overlay and initial skill authored by nanoRSI are original
and contain no upstream code. ALFWorld reference: "ALFWorld: Aligning Text and
Embodied Environments for Interactive Learning" (ICLR 2021, arXiv:2010.03768).
Evaluating this pack requires a Python 3.12 interpreter with alfworld installed
(textworld textgen is incompatible with Python 3.13 under PEP 667); the runner
re-execs itself under that interpreter (NANORSI_ALF_PYTHON).
